WF-01 — Message Router

## Summary

- Inputs: Parsed WhatsApp message payload from WF-00 (phoneNumber, phoneNumberFormatted, messageType, messageContent, rawMessage, contactName, etc.)
- Outputs: Either a silent reject, a deflection WA message, a forced route to WF-21 (for opted-out users) carrying the §2.1 envelope, an admin Slack anomaly alert (for unrecorded-phone interactive taps or STOP/REBOOK keywords), or a call to WF-02 with the §2.1 core envelope.
- **Envelope emission (data-contract-discipline Phase 1 — design.md §2.1):** Every output branch that calls a downstream workflow (WF-02 on the main path, WF-21 on the opted-out re-engagement path) emits the canonical core envelope — `{ phoneNumber, messageType, messageContent, user:{id, phone_number, name, status, slack_channel_id, current_consultation_id}, pendingUser }`. Per the layered principle (slim core + leaf SELECTs for extras), every leaf can read these fields without re-SELECTing the user row.
- State Transitions: none (read-only — does not mutate user state)
- Calls Sub-Workflows: WF-02, WF-21 (for opted_out re-engagement), WF-50 (non-text deflection), WF-51 (admin anomaly alert)
- **User-load gate (SP-11):** After Steps 10–12 load `user` and `pendingUser` and prepare the combined payload, WF-01 explicitly gates on the user-existence triple `(user, pendingUser, messageType)` before calling WF-02. Two anomaly classes are intercepted at the source rather than downstream: (a) `interactive` button taps from an unrecorded phone (bot/spam interaction or DB row deleted after we sent a button); (b) STOP/REBOOK keywords from an unrecorded phone (pre-onboarding STOP edge — eliminates the WF-47 null-user case at the source). Both route to a WF-51 admin alert into `chinmay-admin-commands` (C0A5B0ZE81E) and DO NOT call WF-02. Legitimate cases — user exists, pendingUser exists, or plain-text from a new phone — continue to WF-02 unchanged.

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Start — triggered by another workflow (WF-00) with the parsed message payload.
Step 2: Layer 1 — Country Filter. Check if phoneNumberFormatted starts with allowed country codes ('91' India or '61' Australia).
  - If NOT allowed → set securityCheck='REJECTED', rejectReason='country_not_allowed', silent=true, go to Step 3.
  - If allowed → set securityCheck='PASSED_COUNTRY', go to Step 3.
Step 3: Check: securityCheck == 'REJECTED' (country)?
  - If YES → go to Step 17 (silent reject, end).
  - If NO → go to Step 4.
Step 4: Layer 2 — Non-Text Message Filter. Check messageType against allowed list ['text', 'interactive'].
  - Set messageTypeAllowed = true/false accordingly.
Step 5: Check: messageTypeAllowed == true?
  - If YES → go to Step 6.
  - If NO → go to Step 18 (deflect via WF-50, end).
Step 6: SELECT id, phone_number, status, blocked_reason FROM chinmay_astro.users WHERE phone_number = $phoneNumber AND status IN ('blocked', 'opted_out').
Step 7: Layer 3 — Blacklist evaluation:
  - If a row exists and status='opted_out' → set securityCheck='OPTED_OUT', silent=true.
  - Else if a row exists (status='blocked') → set securityCheck='REJECTED', rejectReason='blacklisted', silent=true.
  - Else → set securityCheck='PASSED_BLACKLIST'.
Step 8: Check: securityCheck == 'REJECTED' (blacklist)?
  - If YES → go to Step 19 (silent reject blacklist, end).
  - If NO → go to Step 9.
Step 9: Check: securityCheck == 'OPTED_OUT'?
  - If YES → build the §2.1 core envelope via the `Build WF-01 Envelope (Opted-Out)` Code node (re-SELECT or carry forward the full user row as needed to fill `user.{id, phone_number, name, status, slack_channel_id, current_consultation_id}`; `pendingUser` is null on this branch). Then call WF-21 with the envelope plus `wasOptedOut: true` and `messageText` so the user is treated as a re-engagement; WF-21 uses `wasOptedOut` to prepend a "Welcome back" acknowledgement. End.
  - If NO → go to Step 10.
Step 10: SELECT phone_number, contact_name, created_at FROM chinmay_astro.pending_users WHERE phone_number = $phoneNumber (look for in-flight onboarding).
Step 11: SELECT id, phone_number, name, date_of_birth, time_of_birth, place_of_birth, status, current_consultation_id, total_consultations, context, created_at, updated_at, last_message_at, awaiting_feedback, slack_channel_id, stage, blocked_at, blocked_by, blocked_reason, feedback FROM chinmay_astro.users WHERE phone_number = $phoneNumber (full user record — projects every column read by downstream nodes / sub-workflows).
Step 12: Prepare combined payload (Prepare User Data):
  - pendingUser = row from Step 10 if any (camelCase mapped: phoneNumber, contactName, createdAt), else null.
  - user = row from Step 11 if any (parse `context` JSON to object; map snake_case columns → camelCase fields: id, phoneNumber, name, dateOfBirth, timeOfBirth, placeOfBirth, status, currentConsultationId, totalConsultations, context, createdAt, updatedAt, lastMessageAt, awaitingFeedback, slackChannelId, stage, blockedAt, blockedBy, blockedReason, feedback), else null.
  - isNewUser = (user is null) AND (pendingUser is null).
  - Carry forward messageId, phoneNumber, contactName, messageType, messageContent, messageContentUpper, rawMessage, timestamp, metadata.
Step 12a: User-Load Gate (Set node, `includeOtherFields=true` so phoneNumber/user/pendingUser/messageType/messageContentUpper pass through to downstream) — classify the combined payload into one of four routing dispositions based on (user, pendingUser, messageType, messageContentUpper):
  - `user` is not null → routing='to_wf02' (existing user — normal flow).
  - `user` is null AND `pendingUser` is not null → routing='to_wf02' (legitimate pre-form state; WF-02 will route PRE_FORM_TEXT / DETAILS_FORM).
  - `user` is null AND `pendingUser` is null AND messageType='text' AND messageContentUpper does NOT match exact `STOP` or `REBOOK` → routing='to_wf02' (legitimate new-user text; WF-02 will route NEW_USER → WF-21; HELP from new user is also fine — WF-21 acks).
  - `user` is null AND `pendingUser` is null AND messageType='interactive' → routing='anomaly_interactive'.
  - `user` is null AND `pendingUser` is null AND messageContentUpper exactly matches `STOP` or `REBOOK` → routing='anomaly_keyword'.
Step 12b: Build WF-01 Envelope (Code node, per design.md §2.1) — emit the canonical core envelope `{ phoneNumber, messageType, messageContent, user:{id, phone_number, name, status, slack_channel_id, current_consultation_id} | null, pendingUser:{id, contact_name} | null }`. Carry forward `messageContentUpper`, `routing`, `messageId`, `timestamp`, `rawMessage` so downstream branches retain routing context. Go to Step 12c.
Step 12c: Check: routing == 'to_wf02'?
  - If YES → go to Step 13 (existing WF-02 call).
  - If NO  → go to Step 12d (anomaly branch).
Step 12d: Build Admin Anomaly Alert (Set node, default `includeOtherFields=false` — emits only the new contract for WF-51) — emit {
    channelId: 'C0A5B0ZE81E',
    messageText: routing == 'anomaly_interactive'
      ? "⚠️ Unexpected button tap from a phone we don’t recognise: +<phoneNumber>. They tapped a button we previously sent, but they’re not registered for a consultation. Likely spam or their record was removed. Content: `<messageContent>`."
      : "⚠️ Received `<messageContentUpper>` from a phone we don’t recognise: +<phoneNumber>. They haven’t started onboarding yet, so there’s nothing to opt out of or rebook. No action taken."
  }. Then call WF-51 (Send Slack Message). End. WF-02 is NOT called. (Message text uses business language only — see [[feedback_admin_message_tone]].)
Step 13: Call WF-02 (User State Router) with the combined payload.
Step 14: End.

Step 17: Silent reject (country) — return {silentReject: true, reason: 'country_not_allowed'}. End.
Step 18: Call WF-50 with phoneNumber and message "Please send text messages only. Images and audio are not supported." End.
Step 19: Silent reject (blacklist) — return {silentReject: true, reason: 'blacklisted'}. End.
